25,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Our yards are a mess of old gear, and trying to switch systems during peak season is a disaster. We need something that fits our actual schedule.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems the board ignores operating costs while cutting capital. Also, separate licenses for add-ons are becoming a financial drain over time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We have a serious accountability gap; last winter's outage was unowned for days. Plus, our project scopes never survive a year of real business changes.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The dispatch tool is ancient because we can't find time to upgrade it, and external data moves left us with errors for a whole year!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are losing our system experts to retirement and can't hire replacements. Moreover, depot supervisors often ignore standard training to keep their own routines.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, if nobody is in charge when things break, that's even worse for the guys in the yard.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, if we keep using external teams for data lifts and they fail, we are paying for mistakes twice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, exactly. We need a single point of accountability and a system that doesn't freeze our ability to adapt.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Servas, does that mean the new system needs to be really easy to learn, or the trainers need to stay longer?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Servas,,"Both, Rin. We cannot rely on a ""visit"" from a trainer if the supervisors just revert to old ways.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Mizuki, would a subscription model help with those operating costs you found?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Not necessarily, Kenji. Bundled agreements are stable, but modular ""add-ons"" are where the costs spiral.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if we can't hire admins, we should avoid any system that requires heavy internal technical management.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Rin,,I just don't want another system that we're too scared to upgrade for ten years!,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, I agree. A system that requires a specialized internal team we cannot hire is a liability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
