50,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"The candidates are A: Tessera, B: Corvus, C: Anchor, and D: Meridian. I lean toward C because they keep engineers on-site through rollout.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"B is modular, which I fear means those climbing renewal costs I saw. A and D are suites, which are more price-stable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"A uses a partner firm for migration, which Rin's data suggests is risky. D has a fixed configuration and a regional service team.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Rin,,"C is on our own servers, but my research shows we skip upgrades because we can't test them. I don't want that again!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Servas,,"A relies on a partner for training, but C has engineers present. However, D's fixed process might be easier for stretched staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, if C is on our servers, does that mean it's harder to update?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, does D's fixed configuration solve the problem of the business changing every few months?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, it might make it more rigid, but it prevents the ""scope creep"" that leads to the failures I found.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Kenji, yes, that's exactly what happened with the dispatch tool. I'm voting against C.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the on-site engineers of C are helpful, but if the supervisors ignore them, it's wasted effort.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"If C is out, D seems better for the yard. A regional service team is better than a distant partner.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"D is a hosted suite, which avoids the modular price hikes of B and the capital risks of C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"D provides a clear support structure and a controlled rollout, which addresses my concerns about ownership.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Rin,,"D is hosted, so we don't have to worry about the ""aging in place"" problem I saw with the dispatch tool!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Servas,,D's fixed configuration reduces the burden on our missing administrators. It is the most sustainable path.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I vote for D.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Asuka,,D is the logical choice.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm with everyone! D!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Servas,,I concur. D it is.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
